 "text": "Property Tax | Sibley County, MN\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nCounty Government\nDepartments\nServices\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nDepartments\nAuditor-Treasurer\nProperty Tax\nProperty Tax\nPer Minnesota Statute, current year tax statements must be mailed annually by March 31st; therefore, you can expect them in your mailbox around the first week of April. They are only mailed once per year.**\n**UPDATE: 2026 tax statements were mailed on Friday, March 20.\nView Tax Statements or Make a Payment\nFor more information on property taxes in Minnesota, refer to the back of your tax statement or click on the links below:\nHelpful Links\nUnderstanding Property Tax\nProperty Tax Refund\nProperty Tax Deferral for Senior Citizens\nState General Levy Tax Info\nLate Payments / Penalties\nhttps://www.sibleycounty.gov/606/delinquent-property-taxes Delinquent Taxes & Tax Forfeiture\nMobile Home Taxes\nTax Payment Reminders\nPROPERTY TAX 101\nBasic Information on how Taxes are calculated, etc:\nTerms and Concepts PDF\nProperty Tax Variation by Property Type PDF\nAdministration PDF\nTax Extension Rates\n2026 TAX EXTENSION RATES PDF\n2025 TAX EXTENSION RATES PDF\n2024 TAX EXTENSION RATES PDF\n2023 TAX EXTENSION RATES PDF\n2022 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2021 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2020 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2019 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2018 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2017 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2016 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2013 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2012 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2011 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2010 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2009 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2008 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2015 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\n2014 Tax Extension Rates (PDF)\nTax Capacities and Market Values by Taxing Authority\n2026 Tax Capacities and Market Values by Taxing Authorities PDF\n2025 Tax Capacities and Market Values by Taxing Authorities PDF\n2024 Tax Capacities and Market Values by Taxing Authorities PDF\n2023 Tax Capacities and Market Values by Taxing Authorities PDF\nGross Tax by Taxing Authority\n2026 Payable Gross Tax by Taxing Authority-Entity PDF\n2025 Payable Gross Tax by Taxing Authority-Entity PDF\n2024 Payable Gross Tax by Taxing Authority-Entity PDF\n2023 Payable Gross Tax by Taxing Authority-Entity PDF\nCity Tax Rate Comparison\nTax Comparison 2026 Payable PDF\nTax Comparison 2025 Payable PDF\nTax Comparison 2024 Payable PDF\nTax Comparison 2023 Payable PDF\nTax Comparison 2022 Payable (PDF)\nTax Comparison 2021 Payable (PDF)\nTax Comparison Report\n2022-2023 TaxComparison PDF\n2021-2022 TaxComparison.pdf PDF\nTaxes Collected\n2022 Taxes Collected PDF\n2021 Taxes Collected.pdf PDF\nDrainage Ditch Reports\nJD15 Radintz Petition for Removal of Benefits Notice PDF\nAdditional Resources\nSibley County Ditch Maps\nInteractive Parcel Map\nView All Additional Resources\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nContact Us\nAuditor-Treasurer\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n400 Court Avenue\n1st Floor Historic Courthouse\nGaylord , MN 55334\n400 Court Avenue 1st Floor Historic Courthouse Gaylord MN 55334\nDirections\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 51\n400 Court Avenue\nGaylord , MN 55334\nPhone: 507-237-4070\nFax: 507-237-4358\nProperty Tax\nEmail Property Tax\nDirectory\nCurrent Year Taxes\nPayment Options\nDelinquent Property Taxes & Tax Forfeiture\nTax Payment Reminders\nMobile Home Taxes\nAgendas & Minutes\nEmployment\nNotify Me®\nElections & Voting\nProperty Tax\nLicenses & Permits\n-->\nContact Us\nSibley County\nGaylord, MN 55334\nPhone: 507-237-7800\nEmail Us\nQuick Links\nLicense Cen